<title>SINGAPORE: Nepal awards diesel to Glencore, kero to Mitsubishi.</title>
<headline>Nepal awards diesel to Glencore, kero to Mitsubishi.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Nepal Oil Corp (NOC) bought by tender 30,000 tonnes each of diesel and kerosene from Swiss trader Glencore and Japan's Mitsibishi Corp, respectively, for May 1-10 deliveries, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 1.0-percent sulphur diesel was purchased at $194 per tonne on a two-port discharge basis to the Indian east coast, cost-and-freight (c-and-f).</p>
<p>The superior kerosene cargo was bought at $204 per tonne, c-and-f east coast.</p>
<p>In its last tender, Nepal bought diesel from German trader Mabanaft at $202.75 per tonne for March 11-20 delivery, c-and-f, and two kerosene cargoes from Dutch trader Vitol at $235-$240 per tonne for March 1-10 and 21-31 deliveries, c-and-f.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
